Thanks for this Torsten!  Also note that a common mistake is for people to try to put in areas into the fixlikes, when really they should be putting in likelihoods for the ranges.

E.g., for a 2-area system

The areas are: A, B (2 total areas)
The ranges are: null, A, B, AB (4 total ranges)

Incorrect: fixlikes = c(11)  (an incorrect attempt to specify range AB)

Correct: fixlikes = c(0001)  (a correct attempt to specify range AB)

For fixing 2 nodes to AB, the corresponding procedure would be:
fixlikes = rbind(c(0001), c(0001))

Use this script to figure out how many ranges/states you have, and in what order (unless you modify the states_list somehow, which is an advanced topic):
http://phylo.wikidot.com/example-biogeobears-scripts#list_of_ranges

Cheers!
Nick

